#---
# purpose: "a plain user function discarding f.(x) drives the same seam disagreement as Enum.each, with no Enum in sight"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# fz-kdt.155's second witness, and the one that says the bug is not about
# `Enum`. `apply_discarding/2` is the whole of `Enum.each`'s step written out
# by hand: call the callable, throw the result away, return something else. One
# lambda reaches it twice -- once named, once after a mailbox round trip has
# erased the name -- so the same grounded call and boxed call meet over one
# construction wrapper.
#
# Nothing about the runtime library is involved, so a fix that leans on
# `Enum.each`'s shape rather than on the seam's own return convention leaves
# this program aborting in `fz_closure_get_capture_ref`.
fn apply_discarding(f, x) do
  f.(x)
  :ok
end

fn main() do
  double = fn (x) -> dbg(x * 2) end
  dbg(apply_discarding(double, 1))

  send(self(), double)
  boxed = receive do f -> f end
  dbg(apply_discarding(boxed, 2))
  dbg(:done)
end
